    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S2864\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the navigation law, in relation to the Irondequoit bay\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThis bill amends the state navigation law governing the operation of\nvessels in Irondequoit Bay, increasing the \"no-wake\" zone in the Bay\nfrom 200 to 300 feet.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nThis legislation increases the distance in Irondequoit bay that\nvessels are permitted to operate in excess of five miles per hour from\n200 to 300 feet. It makes an exception for boats that are enabling a\nwater skier to take off or land. This required buffer zone extends\nfrom the vessel to the shoreline, the channel between Irondequoit Bay\nand Lake Ontario; as well as any dock, pier, raft or float, or\nanchored or moored vessel.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe Irondequoit Bay Harbor Management Law represents a compact between\nthe towns of Irondequoit, Penfield and Webster, all of which surround\nIrondequoit Bay, located in Monroe County. The harbor management plan,\nwhich is based on the recommendations of a 2003 plan constructed by\nthe towns, is a uniform strategy to deal with water surface and\nrelated uses on and around the bay. All three town boards adopted this\ncomprehensive plan in 2008.\n\nSpecifically, the plan establishes requirements and procedures for the\nenvironmental protection and safe recreational use of Irondequoit Bay.\nIn doing so, it works to ensure that development around the Bay occurs\nwithout impacting the significant natural environment, thereby\nprotecting water quality.  Further, the plan regulates the operation\nof vessels ensuring safety for all; and also, addresses water surface\nuses and ancillary uses; docking, boat storage and moorings; and\nenforcement, violations and penalties.\n\nOne such provision of this plan involves amending the state navigation\nlaw to increase the \"no-wake\"/5 mile-per-hour zone from 200 feet off\nthe shore to 300 feet. This buffer zone also extends to docks, piers\nand anchored vessels. The measure aims to provide a safer environment\nfor those living on and enjoying this treasured waterway.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
